[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver.py: Implemented SemVer 2.0.0 interface: dataclass error hierarchy with __str__ diagnostics, ComparatorOp enum, frozen data types (Version with format/is_prerelease, VersionRange, PackageDependency, PackageRelease, ResolutionOutcome), and VersionEngine/PackageRepository/DependencySolver protocol declarations matching low/semver_solver.pyi.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Implemented semver engine, repository, and backtracking solver: strict SemVer 2.0.0 parse_version with leading-zero rejection, precedence comparison ignoring build metadata, range compilation supporting comparators (whitespace-separated, no commas), caret/tilde/wildcard/hyphen/union forms with partial-version and malformed-syntax rejection, prerelease-aware satisfies, descending-precedence repository indexing with PackageNotFoundError, and MRV/lexical-tie-break backtracking resolver that reports ResolutionConflictError (conflicting packages + derivation explanation) without leaking PackageNotFoundError.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Implement full pretense module for the SemVer solver: model state with precedence/range/resolution oracles, nine transitions covering all engine, repository, and solver operations with contracted error branches, shared-state fake factory, fake unit tests, dispatch-driven real implementation tests, and Hypothesis fuzz SUT.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Change header claims contracted error branches are modeled, but no error transition exists: the transitions for parse_version (lines 570-588), parse_range (lines 608-624), get_releases (lines 679-694), and resolve (lines 730-752) declare outcomes only via ctx.returns fake-return helpers _return_parse_version (line 419), _return_parse_range (line 428), _return_get_releases (line 448), and _return_resolve (line 460) that hand back Raised(...) sentinels, so the error branches mandated by low/semver_solver_impl.pyi are never declared with ctx.raises plus an antecedent guard and are unreachable when the real SUT is dispatched: VersionEngine.parse_version must raise InvalidVersionError on grammar mismatch and leading-zero input, VersionEngine.parse_range must raise InvalidRangeError on empty/whitespace-only text, bare partial versions, and comma-delimited comparators, PackageRepository.get_releases must raise PackageNotFoundError for an unregistered name, and DependencySolver.resolve must raise ResolutionConflictError rather than letting PackageNotFoundError escape. Separately, _verify_resolve (lines 545-566) calls check.get(VersionEngine) at line 552, treating the pretense check object as a singleton locator, which raises KeyError 'No singleton registered for type VersionEngine' whenever the verification runs without a state-machine singleton table; the oracle verification must use the dispatched target SUT or the model oracle already present in the state instead of resolving services from check.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Model contracted error branches as dedicated transitions declared with ctx.raises and mutually exclusive recognizers/antecedents: parse_version_error (InvalidVersionError for grammar mismatch and leading zeroes), parse_range_error (InvalidRangeError for empty, bare partial, and comma-delimited ranges), get_releases_error (PackageNotFoundError for unregistered names), resolve_error (ResolutionConflictError for unsatisfiable dependencies). Success transitions now recognize only model-valid inputs and no longer emit Raised return sentinels, and real-mode error scenarios dispatch the error transitions directly. _verify_resolve now validates selected versions against the model range oracle already held in state instead of resolving VersionEngine from check.get, eliminating the KeyError on singleton lookup.
