[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Dispatch real-mode error scenarios by their contracted interface operation names (parse_version, parse_range, get_releases, resolve) instead of invented alias keys, so the mutually exclusive recognizers select the registered ctx.raises transitions: parse_version_error and parse_range_error recognize model-invalid text (try_parse_version/try_parse_range is None), get_releases_error recognizes names absent from the model repository, and resolve_error recognizes unsatisfiable dependency sets where the model resolution is None. This certifies InvalidVersionError, InvalidRangeError, PackageNotFoundError, and ResolutionConflictError against the real SUT without alias transition keys.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: The Change header claims real-mode error scenarios dispatch the new ctx.raises transitions, but the real-mode class still dispatches by operation name only, and name-based dispatch pins a single registered transition per operation and aborts when that one transition's own guard or recognizer rejects the arguments, so the sibling ctx.raises transitions are never candidates: 'parse_version' at lines 1002 and 1006 aborts with 'Argument generation/recognition failed' because the success transition's recognizer try_parse_version(text) is not None excludes invalid text, 'parse_range' at lines 1048, 1052, and 1056 aborts the same way because its recognizer try_parse_range(text) is not None excludes invalid ranges, and 'get_releases' at line 1105 aborts with 'Requirement failed' because the success transition added the antecedent guard requiring at least one registered package, all before the corresponding ctx.raises branches can be selected. Because dispatch_transition accepts either a target or a name, the error scenarios must dispatch against the real singleton target (the VersionEngine, PackageRepository, and DependencySolver instances already constructed in setUp) so the framework selects among the multiple transitions declared for the same operation using their mutually exclusive recognizers, or verify the real services directly; with name-only dispatch the contracted error behavior of low/semver_solver_impl.pyi stays uncertified: VersionEngine.parse_version must raise InvalidVersionError for grammar mismatch and leading zeroes, VersionEngine.parse_range must raise InvalidRangeError for empty/whitespace-only, bare partial versions, and comma-delimited comparators, PackageRepository.get_releases must raise PackageNotFoundError for unregistered names, and DependencySolver.resolve must raise ResolutionConflictError rather than letting PackageNotFoundError escape.
