[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: The Change header claims dispatch_transition enumerates both sibling transitions whenever a real operation target is supplied, but passing the interface attributes VersionEngine.parse_version (lines 997, 1001), VersionEngine.parse_range (lines 1043, 1047, 1051), PackageRepository.get_releases (line 1100), and DependencySolver.resolve (line 1124) resolves to a single registered transition for that operation name and aborts at its recognizer before the sibling ctx.raises transition is ever considered, still leaving InvalidVersionError, InvalidRangeError, PackageNotFoundError, and ResolutionConflictError uncertified; these scenarios must dispatch against the bound real service instances (self.engine, self.repository, self.solver) rather than the class-level interface descriptors, or assert on the real services directly. The same change also converted the model return providers into assertions: _return_get_releases (lines 446-449) now asserts releases is not None, and _return_resolve (lines 457-463) now asserts outcome is not None, but when the fuzz driver replays an argument that lies outside the success recognizer's admitted domain (an absent package name or an unsatisfiable dependency set) it still invokes the success transition's return provider, so a bare AssertionError crashes the run; the return providers must be total functions of the model state that yield the model outcome for any replayed argument, handling the absent-name and unsatisfiable cases in the model without asserting.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Dispatch real-mode error scenarios against the bound real service instances constructed in setUp (self.engine.parse_version, self.engine.parse_range, self.repository.get_releases, self.solver.resolve) rather than class-level interface descriptors, so the framework enumerates the sibling transitions for the operation and selects the ctx.raises branch via mutually exclusive recognizers, certifying InvalidVersionError, InvalidRangeError, PackageNotFoundError, and ResolutionConflictError. Also made every model return provider total instead of asserting: _return_parse_version, _return_parse_range, _return_get_releases, and _return_resolve now yield the model outcome (including a Raised sentinel carrying the contracted exception) for any replayed argument outside the success recognizer's domain, so fuzz replay of absent names or unsatisfiable dependency sets cannot raise a bare AssertionError.
