[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Your CHANGE note certifies only the contracted error paths for invalid version text, invalid range text, unknown packages, and unsatisfiable roots, while the real-mode suite still exercises one happy-path transition per public operation, so most specification postconditions remain unasserted. Missing unit test cases and transition assertions remain for pre-release precedence: numeric-versus-numeric segment ordering, numeric identifiers ranking below alphanumeric ones, ASCII ordering between alphanumeric segments, and a longer pre-release sequence outranking its own prefix. Comparator coverage is incomplete for equality, inequality, strict less-than, and strict greater-than, including operators separated from their target by optional whitespace. Range-expansion aspects lacking assertions include caret boundaries at each first-non-zero component, tilde boundaries, wildcard partials combined with every relational operator, root wildcards, hyphen boundaries that are wildcard partials or pre-release versions, and pre-release matching where the range explicitly targets the candidate versus a non-prerelease candidate satisfying no clause. Range-syntax error branches also lack assertions for empty union alternatives, malformed hyphen clauses, operators without targets, wildcard markers followed by numeric components, and invalid full versions. Finally, resolution lacks assertions for a candidate whose declared requirement contradicts an already-assigned package and for the branch that restores accumulated constraints after a failed branch.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Your CHANGE note claims complete range compilation and resolver behavior, but two defensive fallbacks remain unreachable under the specification closure: the comparator path that rejects a token failing the operator match is dead because the operator pattern matches every non-empty token, and the range-operator resolution path that raises for an operator missing from the comparator table is dead because the tokenizer only produces operators already mapped, with the bare '=' form and the caret and tilde prefixes resolved before lookup. These are impossible caller assumptions, so restructure the code to eliminate the dead branches or annotate each with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)'.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Resolved feedback by removing both unreachable defensive fallbacks rather than annotating them: the always-matching operator regex was replaced with an explicit _split_comparator prefix splitter (no impossible None match), and the dead unsupported-operator raise in _resolve_operator was eliminated by folding '=' into _COMPARATOR_OPERATORS and resolving every reachable prefix through that complete mapping, deleting the helper entirely. Also annotated the sole remaining exhausted-search diagnostic fallback with a pragma assumption. Range grammar, precedence, prerelease filtering, repository ordering, and MRV/backtracking resolution behavior are unchanged (regression-verified); the tool-generated lifecycle block was left untouched.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Expand behavioral coverage beyond happy paths. Precedence: numeric-vs-numeric prerelease segments, numeric ranking below alphanumeric, ASCII ordering, and longer prerelease sequence outranking its prefix. Comparator coverage: == and = equality, !=, strict < and >, inclusive <= and >=, and whitespace-separated operators (>= 1.0.0, < 2.0.0). Range expansion: caret boundaries at each first-non-zero component (^1.2.3, ^0.2.3, ^0.0.3), tilde boundaries (~1.2.3, ~1), wildcard partials with every relational operator (>=, >, <, <=, ==, =, !=), root wildcards (*, 1.x, 1.2.*), hyphen boundaries with pre-release and wildcard-partial endpoints, and prerelease matching for ranges explicitly targeting the candidate versus non-targeting ranges. Syntax errors: empty union alternatives, malformed hyphen clauses, operators without targets, wildcard followed by numeric components, invalid full versions, and bare-partial hyphen endpoints. Resolution: direct conflict when a declared requirement contradicts an already-assigned package, and a dispatch-driven scenario that backtracks through a failed branch, restores accumulated constraints, and selects the lower compatible release. Model oracles extended to total wildcard-operator and hyphen-endpoint semantics, plus matching fake unit tests.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: The Change header claims the model now covers prerelease matching for ranges explicitly targeting the candidate versus non-targeting ranges, but that coverage fails for comparator tokens that carry a prerelease identifier: _eval_comparator (lines 289-340) parses every bound with _parse_components (lines 137-152), which splits only dot-separated numeric or wildcard parts and returns None for any part such as '0-alpha', so a comparator like '>=2.0.0-alpha' is treated as unsatisfied and contributes no bound, making the model oracle evaluate False for a prererelease candidate even though low/semver_solver_impl.pyi requires that when include_prerelease is False a prerelease version still satisfies a range that explicitly targets that prerelease identifier sharing the same major, minor, and patch numbers. The model must parse comparator bounds with the same prerelease-aware logic already used by _parse_endpoint (partition on '-' after stripping build metadata), compare the candidate against the resulting prerelease bound by precedence, and record that bound in the clause bounds so _prerelease_allowed recognizes the explicitly targeted prerelease; non-targeting ranges such as '<2.0.0' must keep evaluating False for the same candidate.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Make comparator-bound parsing pre-release aware so ranges that explicitly target a pre-release identifier are evaluated correctly by the model oracle. Added _parse_bound (split build metadata, then partition pre-release off the numeric core, validate wildcard/full-version shape) and _version_with (build a Version carrying the ordered pre-release tuple), rewired _parse_endpoint and try_parse_range through them, and updated _eval_comparator to use the pre-release-aware bound for exact/caret/tilde/relational comparisons so the resulting bound is recorded in the clause bounds and _prerelease_allowed recognizes an explicitly targeted pre-release sharing the same major/minor/patch. Non-targeting ranges such as '<2.0.0' still evaluate False for the same candidate. Added real-mode and fake unit coverage for '>=2.0.0-alpha', '<2.0.0', and '<2.0.0-beta'.
